/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.1 Classification and Calorific Value of Fuels) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A fuel is a combustible carbonaceous substance that releases substantial thermal energy) Tj
T*
(upon reaction with oxygen.) Tj
T*
(* Classification: Solid \(Coal, Wood\), Liquid \(Petroleum, Diesel, Ethanol\), Gaseous) Tj
T*
(\(Natural gas, LPG, Biogas\).) Tj
T*
(* Calorific Value: Quantity of heat liberated by complete combustion of a unit) Tj
T*
(quantity of fuel:) Tj
T*
(1. Higher / Gross Calorific Value \(HCV / GCV\): Total heat released when combustion) Tj
T*
(products, including water vapor, are cooled to standard room temperature \(15 deg C\),) Tj
T*
(capturing the latent heat of condensation of steam.) Tj
T*
(2. Lower / Net Calorific Value \(LCV / NCV\): Practical heat available when steam escapes) Tj
T*
(with flue gases without condensing:) Tj
T*
(LCV = HCV - [ Latent Heat of Steam * Mass of Hydrogen * 9 ]) Tj
T*
(LCV = HCV - [ 587 * \(9 * H / 100\) ] kcal/kg = HCV - [ 52.83 * H ] kcal/kg \(or 2.45 MJ/kg) Tj
T*
(in SI units\).) Tj
T*
(* Dulong's Empirical Formula: Estimates gross calorific value from elemental ultimate) Tj
T*
(analysis:) Tj
T*
(HCV = \(1 / 100\) * [ 8,080 * C + 34,500 * \(H - O / 8\) + 2,240 * S ] kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(\(O/8 accounts for combined hydrogen already bonded as water\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.2 Determination of Calorific Value via Bomb Calorimeter) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Apparatus: Heavy stainless steel cylindrical bomb lined with platinum/enamel.) Tj
T*
(Weighed fuel \(~0.8-1.0 g\) in crucible ignited electrically via iron/fuse wire under) Tj
T*
(25-30 atm pure O2 pressure, immersed in weighed water \(W\) contained in copper) Tj
T*
(calorimeter of water equivalent \(w\).) Tj
T*
(* Calculation Formula:) Tj
T*
(HCV = [ \(W + w\) * \(T2 - T1 + delta t\) - \(Cooling + Wire + Acid Corrections\) ] / Mass of) Tj
T*
(Fuel \(m\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.3 Coal Analysis: Proximate vs. Ultimate) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Proximate Analysis \(Physical empirical testing\):) Tj
T*
(1. Moisture \(%\): Heated at 105-110 deg C for 1 hour: % Moisture = \(Loss in mass / Mass) Tj
T*
(of coal\) * 100.) Tj
T*
(2. Volatile Matter \(%\): Heated in covered crucible at 925 +/- 20 deg C for 7 minutes: %) Tj
T*
(VM = \(Loss in mass - Moisture\) / Mass * 100.) Tj
T*
(3. Ash \(%\): Heated in open crucible at 700-750 deg C until constant weight: % Ash =) Tj
T*
(\(Mass of residue / Mass\) * 100.) Tj
T*
ET

