/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 4.4 Knocking, Octane and Cetane Ratings) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Knocking in SI \(Spark-Ignition Petrol\) Engines: Pre-ignition/auto-ignition of) Tj
T*
(unburned fuel-air mixture ahead of flame front, producing sharp metallic pinging,) Tj
T*
(power loss, and cylinder wear.) Tj
T*
(* Octane Number: Measure of knock resistance in petrol engines. Standard scale:) Tj
T*
(Iso-octane \(2,2,4-trimethylpentane, highly branched, knock resistant\) assigned 100;) Tj
T*
(n-heptane \(straight-chain, knocks violently\) assigned 0.) Tj
T*
(* Cetane Number: Measure of ignition delay in CI \(Compression-Ignition Diesel\)) Tj
T*
(engines. Standard scale: Cetane \(n-hexadecane, short ignition delay\) assigned 100;) Tj
T*
(alpha-methylnaphthalene \(long ignition delay\) assigned 0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 1: Bomb Calorimeter Experimental Calculation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: In a Bomb Calorimeter test, 0.85 g of coal burned completely, causing the) Tj
T*
(temperature of 2,200 g of water in a calorimeter \(water equivalent w = 450 g\) to rise) Tj
T*
(from 24.20 deg C to 26.85 deg C. Cooling correction delta t = 0.05 deg C; fuse wire) Tj
T*
(correction = 12.0 cal; sulfur acid correction = 25.0 cal; cotton thread correction = 5.0) Tj
T*
(cal. If coal contains 5.0% hydrogen, calculate HCV and LCV in kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Effective Temperature Rise \(Delta T\):) Tj
T*
(Delta T = \(T2 - T1\) + delta t = \(26.85 - 24.20\) + 0.05 = 2.65 + 0.05 = 2.70 deg C.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Total Water Equivalent:) Tj
T*
(W + w = 2,200 g + 450 g = 2,650 g.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Total Corrections:) Tj
T*
(Total Corrections = 12.0 + 25.0 + 5.0 = 42.0 calories.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Calculate Gross Calorific Value \(HCV\):) Tj
T*
(HCV = [ \(W + w\) * Delta T - Corrections ] / m) Tj
T*
(HCV = [ \(2,650 * 2.70\) - 42.0 ] / 0.85 = [ 7,155 - 42.0 ] / 0.85 = 7,113 / 0.85 =) Tj
T*
(8,368.24 cal/g = 8,368.2 kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Calculate Net Calorific Value \(LCV\) with H = 5.0%:) Tj
T*
(LCV = HCV - [ 52.83 * %H ] = 8,368.2 - [ 52.83 * 5.0 ] = 8,368.2 - 264.15 = 8,104.05) Tj
T*
(kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(Final Results: HCV = 8,368.2 kcal/kg | LCV = 8,104.1 kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
