([SOLVED PROBLEM 2: Dulong's Theoretical Calorific Value Calculation]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Ultimate analysis of a coal sample yields: Carbon = 82.0%, Hydrogen = 6.0%,) Tj
T*
(Oxygen = 4.0%, Nitrogen = 2.0%, Sulfur = 1.5%, Ash = 4.5%. Calculate HCV and LCV in) Tj
T*
(kcal/kg using Dulong's formula.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Available Hydrogen:) Tj
T*
(Available H = H - \(O / 8\) = 6.0 - \(4.0 / 8\) = 6.0 - 0.50 = 5.50%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Apply Dulong's Formula:) Tj
T*
(HCV = \(1 / 100\) * [ 8,080 * C + 34,500 * \(H - O/8\) + 2,240 * S ]) Tj
T*
(HCV = \(1 / 100\) * [ \(8,080 * 82\) + \(34,500 * 5.50\) + \(2,240 * 1.5\) ]) Tj
T*
(HCV = \(1 / 100\) * [ 662,560 + 189,750 + 3,360 ] = \(1 / 100\) * [ 855,670 ] = 8,556.7) Tj
T*
(kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate LCV:) Tj
T*
(LCV = HCV - [ 52.83 * %H ] = 8,556.7 - [ 52.83 * 6.0 ] = 8,556.7 - 316.98 = 8,239.7) Tj
T*
(kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: HCV = 8,556.7 kcal/kg | LCV = 8,239.7 kcal/kg.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: Proximate Analysis Quantification]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: 2.00 g of coal was heated at 105 deg C for 1 hour; residue weighed 1.88 g. The) Tj
T*
(same sample in a covered crucible was heated at 925 deg C for 7 minutes; residue weighed) Tj
T*
(1.24 g. Burning completely in an open crucible yielded 0.22 g of ash. Calculate) Tj
T*
(proximate analysis percentages.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: % Moisture:) Tj
T*
(Loss in weight = 2.00 - 1.88 = 0.12 g.) Tj
T*
(% Moisture = \(0.12 / 2.00\) * 100 = 6.0%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: % Volatile Matter:) Tj
T*
(Total loss at 925 deg C = 2.00 - 1.24 = 0.76 g.) Tj
T*
(Loss due to volatile matter alone = 0.76 - 0.12 \(moisture\) = 0.64 g.) Tj
T*
(% Volatile Matter = \(0.64 / 2.00\) * 100 = 32.0%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: % Ash:) Tj
T*
(Residue = 0.22 g.) Tj
T*
(% Ash = \(0.22 / 2.00\) * 100 = 11.0%.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: % Fixed Carbon:) Tj
T*
(% Fixed Carbon = 100 - [ 6.0 + 32.0 + 11.0 ] = 100 - 49.0 = 51.0%.) Tj
T*
(Final Report: Moisture = 6.0% | VM = 32.0% | Ash = 11.0% | Fixed Carbon = 51.0%.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
