(3%, N2 = 2%. Calculate the minimum volume of atmospheric air \(containing 21% O2 by) Tj
T*
(volume\) required for complete combustion of 1 m^3 of this gas.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Combustion Chemical Equations per m^3:) Tj
T*
(1. CH4 + 2 O2 -> CO2 + 2 H2O. O2 required = 0.75 * 2 = 1.50 m^3.) Tj
T*
(2. C2H6 + 3.5 O2 -> 2 CO2 + 3 H2O. O2 required = 0.15 * 3.5 = 0.525 m^3.) Tj
T*
(3. CO + 0.5 O2 -> CO2. O2 required = 0.05 * 0.5 = 0.025 m^3.) Tj
T*
(4. H2 + 0.5 O2 -> H2O. O2 required = 0.03 * 0.5 = 0.015 m^3.) Tj
T*
(5. N2 is non-combustible.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Total Theoretical Oxygen Required:) Tj
T*
(Total O2 = 1.50 + 0.525 + 0.025 + 0.015 = 2.065 m^3 of pure O2 per m^3 of gas.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Calculate Minimum Air Volume \(Air is 21% O2 by volume\):) Tj
T*
(Volume of Air = Total O2 * \(100 / 21\) = 2.065 * 4.762 = 9.833 m^3.) Tj
T*
(Final Answer: Exactly 9.833 m^3 of air is required per m^3 of fuel gas.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
